@* A Villain the player made and the GM now holds, drawn back to the player as their nemesis.

   **The owner's ruling of 2026-10-01: the name and an effect, never the sheet.** "Just give them
   something they can see and go 'holy crap'" — so the name surfaces out of drifting smoke while
   two slit-pupilled eyes open behind it, and the stats stay the GM's. The owner's choices, in
   order: specimen B's surfacing name (2026-10-02), then the second pitch's eyes A over it; always
   the Villain's night palette; either side may still end the membership.

   **Always night, whatever the reader's screen is.** `theme.css` gives `.nemesis` the villain-dark
   token set in every state, so this block is a window into somebody else's game on a Hero's page
   in daylight. Nothing here names a colour; the tokens do.

   **The eyes are HTML, not SVG, and that is what makes them smooth.** Each is an element cut to an
   almond by `clip-path`, its pupil a pseudo-element; the glow is one pre-blurred element behind
   them. So the blink is a composited `transform` and the glow a composited `opacity` — the first
   cut animated SVG groups under a blur filter, which repainted the blur on every frame.

   **The name stays legible at rest and the smoke never crosses it.** Under reduced motion `app.css`
   switches every animation here off outright: the eyes rest open, the glow is steady, the name is
   clear and the smoke still. `ProofPages.TheNemesis` drives this in a browser beside three broken
   twins. *@

<div class="nemesis">
    <span class="nemesis-eyes" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="nemesis-glow"></span>
        <span class="nemesis-eye nemesis-eye-left"></span>
        <span class="nemesis-eye nemesis-eye-right"></span>
    </span>
    <span class="nemesis-veil" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="nemesis-veil nemesis-veil-far" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <span class="nemesis-kicker">Your nemesis</span>
    <b class="nemesis-name">@Name</b>
    <span class="nemesis-who">@Who</span>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What the Villain is called — the label it was last sent under.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Name { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>The game that holds it, or null where the campaign has since been deleted.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Campaign { get; set; }

    private string Who => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Campaign)
        ? "Yours once. The GM holds it now."
        : $"Yours once. The GM of {Campaign} holds it now.";
}
